From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 01:06:21 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] fds-carts

Famicom Disk System games are drawn as one yellow Disk Card in the
retro bitmap renderer (ADR 0054). The proportions are measured on the
Wikimedia Commons photos of a Zelda no Densetsu disk (Poirier273,
CC BY 2.5) and a blank disk (Evan-Amos, public domain): seated at
240x282 (312x367 drawn), the top edge stepping up at both corners and
round the centre tab, the raised U panel with the head window and the
hub, the write-protect holes and side notches, a wide label well over
the lower part and the NINTENDO moulding along the bottom. The yellow
ff c4 00 is the median of the blank disk's plastic in Evan-Amos'
photo; a shell colour chosen in Config/cart_shell.txt still wins. Most
yellow disks have no shutter (only a later series of five games did),
so none is drawn.

The outline and relief are ours (fds_cart.svg, fds_cart_detail.svg),
lit into fds_neutral.png by examples/retro_neutrals.rs; every other
neutral regenerates byte for byte.
